# CEO's OS — Release Gates

## Purpose

Define minimum conditions to close a phase, stage files for commit, or recommend push to `origin/main`.

Release gates protect CEO's OS from mixed commits, silent regressions, test weakening, and undocumented cross-module changes.

## Mandatory Git Checks

Before closing any execution phase, run:

```text
git status --short
git diff --stat
git diff --name-only
git ls-files --others --exclude-standard
git log --oneline -5
git log --oneline origin/main..HEAD
```

Adapt commands to PowerShell on Windows or Bash/Zsh on macOS/Linux. The analytical result matters, not the shell syntax.

## Forbidden Git Practices

- `git add .`
- Including `backend-server.err` in any commit
- Committing unreviewed generated artifacts (dist, logs, local DB)
- Mixed commits without justification (docs + unrelated code + tests)
- Pushing with dirty working tree beyond approved noise (`backend-server.err` only when policy allows)
- Amending pushed commits unless explicitly authorized and safe per project rules
- Force push to `main` unless explicitly authorized

## Validation by Change Type

### Document-only phases

- Only allowed documentation/rule files changed
- No `src/`, `backend/`, `tests/`, CSS, `package.json`, or workflows touched
- No extra untracked files outside whitelist
- Markdown coherent; no duplicate sections from idempotent re-run
- Atomic commit message matches scope
- No commit/push in phase unless explicitly authorized

### JSON files

- `node -e "JSON.parse(...)"` or equivalent validation passes
- No duplicate keys introduced on idempotent re-run
- Golden Dataset expected outputs not changed without separate authorized task

### Frontend code changes

- `npm run build` passes when frontend touched
- Relevant unit tests pass
- E2E when critical route or auth flow affected
- Visual smoke when UI layout affected
- No NaN/Infinity/undefined in user-visible financial outputs
- Demo/fallback labelled where user-facing

### Backend/API changes

- Relevant integration tests pass
- Permission and organizationId review completed
- Audit event behavior reviewed for mutations
- No secret in logs or error responses
- Migrations follow migration safety rule (new versioned file; no silent edit of applied migration)

### Critical calculation changes

- Compared against `docs/testing/golden_inputs.json`
- Checked against `docs/testing/FORMULA_REGISTRY.md`
- No tolerance widening to pass tests
- No test weakening
- Source-of-truth documented if changed
- Human review required for financial/compliance positioning

## Phase Closure Requirements

Every closed phase must report:

- files changed (full list)
- files explicitly not touched
- tests run (commands and result)
- risks identified (P0/P1/P2/P3)
- whether HANDOFF_STATE was generated
- recommended next step and prompt
- pending commit/push status

## Multiplatform Validation

Validation commands must be adapted to the host operating system when necessary.

Do not treat shell syntax incompatibility as a project failure.

Treat the analytical validation result as the source of truth.

## Metrics for Phase Success

| Metric | Pass condition |
|---|---|
| Scope adherence | Only allowed files modified |
| Git hygiene | Atomic commits; no `git add .` |
| Test integrity | No weakened assertions or golden outputs |
| Security | organizationId and permissions reviewed if applicable |
| Truthfulness | Demo/fallback not sold as real |
| Idempotency | Re-run does not duplicate rules or sections |

## Stop Conditions

Stop before declaring phase complete if:

- validation matrix not run for change type
- unexpected files in diff
- golden mismatch unresolved
- cross-tenant or permission ambiguity open
- high-risk diff without explicit approval
